INT. FLORIST'S COLD ROOM - NIGHT

Buckets of white lilies, rows of roses in plastic sleeves. Breath fogs. A compressor hums.

DETECTIVE IMANI BRAITHWAITE-SOTO (40s, long coat) stands at the doorway, gun lowered. Across the aisle, TOBIAS "TOBY" ABERNETHY-KWON (30s, florist's apron, shears in hand) stands motionless among the lilies. Behind him, half hidden by a rack, SERAFINA MOREAU-ODE (30s, wedding dress under a parka) crouches. And in the corner, CALLUM DRAYTON (50s, wet suit jacket), the groom, lies on the floor, hand pressed to his side.

IMANI
Put down the shears.

TOBY
I'm not holding them against anyone.

SERAFINA
(from behind the rack)
He's telling the truth.

IMANI
Then who stabbed him?

CALLUM
(through his teeth)
She did.

Everyone looks at the rack. Serafina rises slowly, empty-handed. Toby steps in front of her.

TOBY
He came at her. She was defending herself.

IMANI
Mr. Abernethy-Kwon, step aside.

TOBY
No.

IMANI
(to Serafina)
Ms. Moreau-Ode, is that true?

SERAFINA
Yes.

CALLUM
(to Imani)
She's lying.

IMANI
Mr. Drayton, don't move. Help is coming.

Callum lets his head fall back among the lilies. Toby lowers the shears and lays them on a bucket. He takes Serafina's hand. Imani holsters her gun and kneels beside Callum, pressing her palm over his hand to hold the wound.

IMANI (CONT'D)
(quietly)
Stay with me.

Far off, a siren rises.
